  "notes": [
    "u_{j}_{spec} is the residual of the issuance equation in month t (contemporaneous): it is the issuance innovation to be purged of fiscal news, never a control.",
    "All three equations of a spec share the same sample (needed for the joint LP).",
    "Units: fraction of lagged 12-month GDP (stock spec: fraction of lagged class stock).",
    "maturity_lead1_*: debt service due in t+1 known at the end of t-1; security-level from 2010-02, proxied by the schedule due in t+1 before (maturity_lead1_source).",
    "IPCA of t-1 enters at lag 1 (released around day 10 of t); IBC-Br at lag 2 (released ~45 days later).",
    "base_rt: pseudo-real-time forecast errors, coefficients estimated through t-1, from the month in which the training sample reaches twice the number of regressors.",
    "The ramp spec replaces R by NTN-B + NTN-C (R equation only)."
  ]
